<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="016" project="spaarkeai-compose-r8">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-S06 — Save-outcome enum on the wire; no HTTP 200 with nothing written</title>
    <phase>1 Track S — Save Reliability (P0, ships alone)</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Adds a field to a public response contract consumed by the client; it is the structural fix the whole project's "no lying" criterion depends on.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Designing a closed outcome taxonomy that must cover every terminal state across two write paths, and that the gate (task 031) will assert against — a contract that is expensive to get wrong.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Touches ComposeService, ComposeEndpoints and the client reducer; tasks 011/019/020 all consume this contract.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, frontend, compose, save-path, contract</tags>
    <estimated-effort>6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    A total write failure can currently present to the user as HTTP 200 "Saved ✓". BuildContainerFailedResult
    returns a failed-step result, ExecuteSaveAsync maps it to Results.Ok, and SaveComposeDocumentResponse has NO
    CompletionState field at all — so the client dispatches saveSucceeded without ever checking whether
    documentSpeId came back non-empty.

    Define a CLOSED save-outcome enum, put it on the response, and make the client route on it. This is the
    contract the fidelity gate's outcome-honesty assertion (task 031) will verify.
  </prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the Compose save pipeline end-to-end (client trigger → endpoint → SaveAsync → SPE write → Dataverse promote) and in ProblemDetails conventions. Follow ADR-001 and ADR-049.</role>

  <goal>
    Every save terminates in exactly one member of a closed outcome enum, that member crosses the wire on
    SaveComposeDocumentResponse, and the client's rendered result is derived from it. A failed write can no
    longer render as success.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      design.md §3 S-6 and §3.1. ADR-049's third amendment (task 060) makes "every save terminates in a defined
      outcome" a STANDING invariant that no future amendment may trade away — this task is where that becomes
      real. The enum is also what task 020's telemetry emits and what task 031 asserts in the gate.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="primary-edit">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs</file>
      <file role="primary-edit">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ComposeEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="primary-edit">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/types/compose-contracts.ts</file>
      <file role="primary-edit">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeWorkspace.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/IComposeService.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">The enum is a CLOSED set: persisted | persisted-with-warnings | refused-stale | refused-locked | refused-invalid | storage-failed | partially-recorded. Adding a member later is a contract change requiring review. Scope: the save response only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">MUST cover BOTH write paths (ContentModel render path and the transitional op-log path) — an unmapped path is exactly the hole this closes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">`partially-recorded` MUST be used for the real case where SPE bytes landed but the Dataverse promote failed — the user is currently told "failed" while the bytes are persisted.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-049">MUST NOT introduce a new undefined content-refusal. Every refusal maps to a named member. Scope: SaveAsync's terminal paths.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Client MUST derive its rendered result from the outcome, not from HTTP status alone. MUST reuse R7's banner stack (root §11).</constraint>
    <constraint source="bff-extensions">State the Placement Justification in the PR; report publish size vs 44.96 MB.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>compose save contract, ProblemDetails, response DTOs</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-049-compose-shadow-document.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/INTEGRATION-CONTRACTS.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r8/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r8/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor declaration">Declare rigor FULL; load spec.md, CLAUDE.md, ADR-049.</step>
    <step order="1">Enumerate EVERY terminal path in SaveAsync + ExecuteSaveAsync (success, each throw, each guard, each best-effort swallow) and map it to an enum member. Any path that cannot be mapped is a finding — record it.</step>
    <step order="2">Define the enum server-side and add it to SaveComposeDocumentResponse; mirror it in compose-contracts.ts.</step>
    <step order="3">Fix the specific 200-with-nothing-written hole: BuildContainerFailedResult → Results.Ok. A failed-step result MUST NOT map to a bare Ok with a success-shaped body.</step>
    <step order="4">Client: route the rendered result on the outcome; assert documentSpeId presence where the outcome claims persistence.</step>
    <step order="5">Add contract tests: one per enum member, asserting the wire shape and the client's rendered result.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a terminal path cannot be honestly mapped to any of the seven members, STOP and surface it — either the taxonomy is wrong or that path is a latent bug the taxonomy just exposed. Do not add a catch-all member to make the mapping close.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ComposeEndpoints.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/types/compose-contracts.ts</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/contract/Api/ComposeSaveOutcomeContractTests.cs</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r8/notes/save-outcome-path-map.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>SaveComposeDocumentResponse carries the outcome; compose-contracts.ts mirrors it.</criterion>
    <criterion>Every terminal path in SaveAsync/ExecuteSaveAsync maps to exactly one member — documented in the path map note.</criterion>
    <criterion>A container/storage failure NO LONGER returns HTTP 200 with a success-shaped body — proven by test.</criterion>
    <criterion>SPE-written-but-promote-failed returns `partially-recorded`, and the client says so honestly.</criterion>
    <criterion>The client's rendered result derives from the outcome, not HTTP status alone.</criterion>
    <criterion>NEGATIVE: a fully successful save returns `persisted` and renders success — no regression on the happy path.</criterion>
    <criterion>NEGATIVE: no catch-all/"unknown" member exists in the enum.</criterion>
    <criterion>Contract tests cover all seven members.</criterion>
    <criterion>Publish size reported vs 44.96 MB; Placement Justification in the PR.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
</task>
